1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:06,300
A response vehicle drives out of coverage. The
network changes; the session should not.

2
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:12,600
Everything here is a software simulation. No
radios, no satellite, no hardware.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,209
The reactive baseline waits for its link to
fail.

4
00:00:16,209 --> 00:00:20,400
The session goes dark four times: seven point
three two seconds.

5
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:24,253
CONTINUA is the working application around
that problem.

6
00:00:24,253 --> 00:00:26,947
Every panel reads from one engine over a live

7
00:00:26,947 --> 00:00:30,000
socket, and the execution mode is always on
screen.

8
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:37,800
Five steps. Observe: receiver side facts only.
The controller never sees the world's script.

9
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:42,600
Predict: a short horizon on those same facts,
three seconds ahead.

10
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:50,000
Prepare: it warms cellular while Wi-Fi still
carries. Steer: six tenths of a second later.

11
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:55,700
Explain: it records why, at the moment it
decided.

12
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:59,733
Same seed, same trace, only the policy
changed.

13
00:00:59,733 --> 00:01:03,200
Seven point three two seconds becomes zero
point one

14
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:06,600
six, and that remainder is the session
starting up.

15
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:12,140
On the satellite route it holds the session
through the fallback, and spends

16
00:01:12,140 --> 00:01:16,800
four point eight megabytes of satellite where
the baseline spends forty seven.

17
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:21,181
Twenty paired trials say something we did not
expect.

18
00:01:21,181 --> 00:01:24,222
Preparation is what removes the interruption.

19
00:01:24,222 --> 00:01:27,600
Take the predictor out and almost nothing
changes.

20
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:32,161
What CONTINUA adds is the price: the same
continuity at

21
00:01:32,161 --> 00:01:35,593
a third of the cost, a twelfth of the
satellite data.

22
00:01:35,593 --> 00:01:37,600
It loses on application health.

23
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:41,500
Scope. A simulation, not a network.

24
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:46,223
Emulation is unverified here and the kernel
has no MPTCP.

25
00:01:46,223 --> 00:01:50,200
Total loss: ten point six seconds, every
policy.

26
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:56,400
CONTINUA. Predictive network continuity. By
Team Kanban.
